// AWS EC2 Large/GPU Instance Launched (Possible Cryptomining)  [tier: hunt]  ATT&CK: T1496
// Detects launching of large or GPU EC2 instance types frequently abused for cryptomining (RunInstances with p/g/x/large families). Heuristic…
// False positives: Legitimate ML/HPC/big-data workloads using GPU or large instances. Allowlist expected types/accounts.
// Source: rules/impact/ec2-run-instances-resource-hijacking.yml — generated by scripts/build_dist.py; adjust field names to your CloudTrail schema.
eventName=/^RunInstances$/i eventSource=/^ec2\.amazonaws\.com$/i requestParameters.instanceType=/^p2/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^p3/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^p4/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^p5/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^g3/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^g4/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^g5/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^g6/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^x1/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^x2/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^inf1/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^inf2/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^trn1/i or requestParameters.instanceType=/^dl1/i
